<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104517" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρᾰγῳδο-ποιός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tragic poet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				425d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				408b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eutoc.
				<u>in Archim.</u>
			</span></i> iii <i><span class="en">
				p.88
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Po.</u>
				2.29
			</span></i>, etc.:  generally, <i>writer of serious
				poetry</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραγῳδία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), e. g. of Homer, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				605c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				607a
			</span></i>; and of Pindar, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραγῳδιοποιός</span>
			is found in <i><span class="en">
				Metrod.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				831.3
			</span></i>, in codd. BT of <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				223d
			</span></i>, cod. A of <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				607a
			</span></i>, etc., and many codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				64.112
			</span></i>, but is f.l. (in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> at least) for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραγῳδοπ-,</span>
			which codd. give correctly in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cra.</u>
				425d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				408b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				597e
			</span></i>: cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωμῳδοποιός.</span></div>
